# Worktree folder names

When creating a Cursor worktree, name the folder so its purpose is obvious at a glance. Prefer a short kebab-case summary of the task or issue, not a generic or opaque label.

```text
# ❌ BAD
wt-1
fix
temp
giovanni-worktree
issue-42

# ✅ GOOD
fix-tour-locale-404
add-tourazione-cta
refactor-menu-queries
```

If the worktree tracks a GitHub issue, include a readable slug plus the issue number when helpful (e.g. `fix-tour-locale-404-42`).
